## 4. Technical Approach and Technologies

Agralyticx is being developed as a full-stack responsive website using a modular architecture.

- **Frontend:** Modern component-based web architecture with responsive UI/UX
- **Backend:** Server-side application layer for business logic and secure data handling
- **Database:** MongoDB for persistent user, agricultural, profile, request, and communication data
- **Authentication:** Secure user authentication with role-based access
- **AI integration:** Gemini API and supporting AI services **planned** for agricultural assistance, multimodal interaction, and crop analysis
- **Voice:** Speech-to-text and text-to-speech for voice-first farmer interaction
- **External services:** Weather, market-rate, mapping, and other APIs are **designed for integration**, with mock/demo data used where live services are not yet connected
- **Localization:** Centralized multilingual system supporting **English, Urdu, and Pakistani Punjabi**, with **Pakistani Sindhi remaining under validation/future expansion**
- **Development tools:** Claude Sonnet 5 and Claude Sonnet 4.6, ChatGPT, and Antigravity were used mainly for development

The architecture separates authentication, database services, AI, speech, translations, role permissions, and application features into independent modules. User data is tied to authenticated user IDs to keep profiles and private information isolated, with role-based permissions protecting dashboards and backend data.

