## 5. Delivery Plan to Close of Build Phase

The core website structure and UI/UX for all five roles are already built. Remaining work proceeds in the following order:

1. **Backend & Database Integration** — authentication, user profiles, role-based access, persistent data via MongoDB.
2. **Core Feature Integration** — crop analysis, market rates, weather, student/company directories, landowner hiring, transport functionality.
3. **AI & Voice Integration** — Gemini and supporting AI tools, voice input/output, multilingual responses, crop-image analysis.
4. **Messaging & Notifications** — student-company communication, landowner-farmer job notifications, transport requests, language-specific notifications.
5. **Testing & Refinement** — all five roles, authentication, permissions, data persistence, multilingual functionality, responsiveness, AI/voice features.
6. **Final UI/UX Polish & Deployment** — usability and responsiveness improvements, final interface, demonstration/deployment readiness.

**Responsibility:** The development team collectively handles frontend, backend, MongoDB, AI integration, testing, and deployment using Claude Sonnet 5/4.6, ChatGPT, and Antigravity as the primary development tools, with members working in parallel on assigned modules.

---

## Summary

Agralyticx's current MVP demonstrates an implemented, role-based product experience across the full agricultural ecosystem — proving the concept end-to-end through UI/UX — while clearly separating what is live today from what remains on the integration roadmap (backend persistence, AI/voice, real-time messaging, and external live-data APIs). This distinction is intentional: it keeps the reported status accurate for evaluators while showing a credible, incremental path to full production functionality.
